From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 21:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] session: keep routine compositor startup out of the VT

The authenticated handheld transition briefly exposes its dedicated virtual
terminal while the greeter compositor releases DRM and Phoc acquires it.
Phoc already sends its diagnostics through systemd-cat; do not force verbose
wlroots logging for every normal login. Debug sessions can still opt in through
the upstream ~/.phoshdebug hook by adding `-v` to COMPOSITOR_ARGS.

---
 data/phosh-session.in | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/data/phosh-session.in b/data/phosh-session.in
index 2776c71..827b55d 100755
--- a/data/phosh-session.in
+++ b/data/phosh-session.in
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
 COMPOSITOR="@compositor@"
+COMPOSITOR_ARGS=${COMPOSITOR_ARGS:-}
 PHOC_INI="@pkgdatadir@/phoc.ini"
 PHOSH_SESSION_BIN=${PHOSH_SESSION_BIN:-gnome-session}
 
@@ -57,4 +58,4 @@ fi
 
 [ -n "$WLR_BACKENDS" ] || WLR_BACKENDS=drm,libinput
 export WLR_BACKENDS
-exec $SYSTEMD_CAT $DBUS_RUN_SESSION "${COMPOSITOR}" -v -S -C "${PHOC_INI}" -E "${PHOSH_SESSION_BIN} --session=phosh"
+exec $SYSTEMD_CAT $DBUS_RUN_SESSION "${COMPOSITOR}" $COMPOSITOR_ARGS -S -C "${PHOC_INI}" -E "${PHOSH_SESSION_BIN} --session=phosh"
-- 
2.53.0
